35,2,1,talk,Minako,,"I've discovered that a full pass takes over an hour and a half in total, and our definitions of ""done"" vary wildly, which explains why the quality of cleaning is so inconsistent.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings confirm a disparity; the calendar shows frequent absences, and the kitchen usage is heavily concentrated among only a few of us, yet the work is currently shared equally.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"The bathroom grout gets black again in just eleven days, and the house chat shows that almost all our fights are just people reminding others to do their chores!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I found that we are spending about 2,300 yen a month on supplies, often buying duplicates, and the management office charges 4,200 yen an hour for a cleaner.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"I've learned that the previous tenants' permanent division led to them barely speaking, and an outside firm requires us to tidy up before they even arrive.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, your point about usage is critical. If a few people cause most of the mess while others are away, a simple equal split feels unfair and inefficient.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Exactly. It seems we are applying a symmetrical solution to an asymmetrical problem, which naturally breeds the resentment Sakura found in the chat logs.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"Wait, so if the grout gets dirty so fast, does that mean we're cleaning for nothing? That sounds super frustrating!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It does seem a bit discouraging, Sakura, but perhaps we just need a more consistent way to handle it so no one feels they are working in vain.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"I worry that if we focus only on the efficiency of the work, we might forget the spirit of the home. We must choose a path that preserves our friendship.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Servas, I agree, but friendship is often strained by the very unfairness Benjamin mentioned. We need a system that acknowledges the actual time and effort required.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. If we ignore the reality of who is using the space and who is actually present, we are merely scheduling future conflicts rather than solving them.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Sakura,,I just want to stop guessing if the kitchen is going to be gross! Can we pick something that makes it stay clean and stops the fighting?,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I agree, Sakura. Perhaps if we have a clear way to handle the costs and the tasks, we can avoid those reminders that lead to disagreements.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a delicate balance. We must ensure that the structure we choose does not become a wall between us, as it did for those who lived here before.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minako,,"We have a clear picture now: inconsistent standards, unfair usage, and a risk of social friction. Let's move to the options and see which one addresses these facts most effectively.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I agree. We have the data; now we must apply logic to select the option that minimizes resentment and maximizes fairness for everyone involved.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm ready to see the options! I hope there's one that makes the bathroom stay sparkly and keeps everyone happy!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I am looking forward to it as well. Let us choose the path that allows us to continue supporting one another with kindness and a light heart.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"Let us proceed then, keeping in mind that the most efficient system is not always the most harmonious one. I am ready to consider our choices.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
